  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#resolve-a-url\r\n\r\n> Let urlRecord be the result of applying the URL parser to url, with baseURL and encoding\\.\r\n> \r\n> If urlRecord is failure, then return failure\\.\r\n\r\nShould this take validation errors into account? E.g. assigning \"\\0000javascript:alert(1)\" to location.href works as it's only a validation error, not a parsing failure, however, this might be unexpected to page authors.",
